Fictional EP Tracklist

Track 1: Sun-Dog Protocol
- Story & Context: In the observation deck of the Icarus-V, Elias noticed a distorted halo forming around a distant star while his fingers bled into the keys. The sensory detail of the freezing air against the metal bench was interrupted by a sudden containment breach alarm that forced the entire rhythm section to shift into a minor third. "The light is lying to us," he sang, trying to mask the sound of escaping oxygen with the frantic resonance of the lower register.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: A lonely, brilliant parhelion halo glowing intensely over a jagged, icy spaceship hull, dark velvet space background, deep blue and sharp orange light, poetic and isolating, fine art photography style.

Track 2: "Where Is the Oxygen?"
- Story & Context: Mara sits alone in the cargo bay with her contact-mic’d piano, confessing to the empty halls that she intentionally bypassed the pressure valves to hear the sound of air thinning. A sharp, stinging scent of ozone fills the room, marking the moment she realizes the ship’s navigation has been compromised for weeks. She plays a jagged, repetitive motif that mimics the rhythm of a failing heart, whispering, "I only wanted to feel the sky turn cold."
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: A close-up of an ornate, weathered piano internal mechanism bathed in dim red emergency light, dust motes dancing in the air, cinematic bokeh, melancholic and claustrophobic mood.

Track 3: Paranoia Corona
- Story & Context: Years after the Icarus-V reached the void, survivors tell the myth of the ghost-pianist who plays inside the ventilation shafts during the ship's quietest hours. The legend began when a maintenance drone found a set of handwritten scores scattered near the engines, the paper smelling faintly of burnt copper. It is said that if you hear the piano, you are already drifting, with the hook, "The ring of color marks the end of all our clocks," echoing through the steel corridors.
